Prototype Design Pattern is basically used to create templates, where as registry Design Pattern is way to add those
templates in Registry and than if needed we can fetch from registry and make clone of those templates.

1) Create template.
2) Create template in such a way that it follows Dependency Inversion Principle.
3) Create a Registry Class.
4) Use a data structure, basically i use HashMAp to store those templates in Registry.
5) Use basic functionalities of Hashmap to store, get, etc. the object from registry.

TIP: Instead of directly fetching the original object from registry , we should fetch the copy of object. So that,
     original object is not modified. To ensure this, i use clone() method in get() method of registry class.


As here the client is creating the template first and than add it in the Registry. But,if i want that my registry is pre-filled,
than for that, just add the prefilled templates in constructors.